    <!-- Tooltips (main window menus, status bar and tabs) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.New">Creates a new vehicle file. You choose its name and location first (an existing file with the same name is never overwritten). Choose the file paths with the Browse buttons.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Close">Closes the open vehicle file and returns to the empty state (asks first if there are unsaved changes).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.OpenLast">When checked, the vehicle file that was open last is opened when the app starts (nothing is opened if it cannot be found).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Backup">Choose whether to keep a backup copy of the previous contents before "Save All" overwrites a file, and how many copies to keep per file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.LaunchBve5">Launches BVE5 (the first time, you choose the location of the BVE5 exe; asks first if there are unsaved changes).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.LaunchBve6">Launches BVE6 (the first time, you choose the location of the BVE6 exe; asks first if there are unsaved changes).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.OpenSettingsFolder">Opens the folder that contains the settings (settings.json) such as theme, window and font. Deleting it restores the defaults the next time the app starts.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.OpenCrashLogFolder">Opens the folder that contains the records of unexpected stops (CrashLogs). If you have trouble, please send the files in this folder.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.OpenBackupFolder">Opens the folder that contains the backup copies made before "Save All" overwrites files (Backups). There is a separate folder for each vehicle file.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.NewLine">The line ending of the text in the current tab (CRLF is usual on Windows; Mixed means two or more kinds are mixed).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.TabUnsaved">{0}: there are unsaved changes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Tip.RecentMissing">{0} (not found)</sys:String>

