    <sys:String x:Key="VP.SummaryKey">{0} ({1}) is only used in BveTs Vehicle 0.03. It is not used in this version ({2}) (from 1.00 it is written in the BveTs Scenario file).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.AtsInNew">Ats ({0}): in this version ({1}), ATS plugins are written as Ats32 (32-bit) and Ats64 (64-bit). &quot;Ats =&quot; may not be read by BVE.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.Ats32InOld">{0} ({1}) is the BveTs Vehicle 2.00 format. In this version ({2}) BVE reports an error (The key '{3}' is not valid.). Write &quot;Ats =&quot; instead, or change the header to 2.00.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.UnknownKey">&quot;{0}&quot; ({1}) is not a vehicle file key (it may be a typo).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.LineSeparator">, </sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.DuplicateKey">{0} is written {1} times ({2}). BVE reports an error and cannot load the vehicle (an entry with the same key already exists). Keep only one.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.NotKeyValue">Line {0} &quot;{1}&quot; is not in the form &quot;key = path&quot;. BVE reports an error (The key '{1}' is not valid.).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.SummaryMoved">Title, Author, Image and Comment moved to the BveTs Scenario file in BveTs Vehicle 1.00 and later (the current BVE ignores them without an error).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.OldNoBve6">A vehicle with the header {0} cannot be loaded by BVE6 (BVE6 is 64-bit and needs Ats64). To use it with BVE6, change the header to BveTs Vehicle 2.00 and write Ats64.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="VP.NoAts64">Only Ats32 (32-bit) is written and there is no Ats64. BVE6 is 64-bit, so it cannot load this vehicle.</sys:String>
